<p>Newark is a city built on movement. One of the busiest airports in the country sits on its southern edge, Port Newark–Elizabeth moves containers around the clock, and Newark Penn Station puts Manhattan about 20 minutes away by train. All that motion is exactly what makes the best side hustles in Newark work: people, packages and events are always arriving and leaving, and someone has to drive, deliver, staff, clean and fix things along the way.</p>
<p>This guide breaks down 18 side gigs that pay in Newark in 2026, with typical pay ranges, startup costs, the neighborhoods and venues that matter, and the New Jersey tax and licensing rules to know before you start.</p>

